> pine, which you are welcome to if you use pine (or if you'd just like
> to look at them).
> 
And I'll have to update all my pgp versions, because some supportscripts
are used on more then one machine (my .pinerc is usable on almost any
platform, except for the PGP-filters....)

> This is a pretty good point though.. I think I'll look to develop a front
> end to 5.0 which accepts 2.6 style arguments.. I still have to graft the
> 5.0 interface code to the 5.5 guts too.. been meaning to do that 
> for awhile.. geez so many projects, so little time :)

Thought of that, but I lack the time :(
Implementing such a filter is not that difficult (maybe only implement the
options you really need..) but what version should be in your $PATH ?? pgp
5.0 or the filter version ??

> an argument translator doesn't sound too tough, though.. of course I
> haven't looked at 2.6 in awhile, so I might be forgetting it's nature
> a little bit :)

