Dear Onsale As233 owners =],<br>
<br>
&nbsp; If you are wonder what to do as far as redhat for this machines
here it goes.<br>
<br>
1) need arc installed<br>
<br>
2) grab the test milo avanti image from digital.<br>
<br>
<font color="#0000FF"><u><a href="ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Linux-Alpha/Kernels/Test-Milos-2.0.30+/milo-avanti-980606" eudora="autourl">ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Linux-Alpha/Kernels/Test-Milos-2.0.30+/milo-avanti-9</a></font></u><a href="ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Linux-Alpha/Kernels/Test-Milos-2.0.30+/milo-avanti-980606" eudora="autourl"><font color="#000000">80606</a>
<br>
<br>
<br>
copy that to a fat disk as avanti and then linload.exe also<br>
<br>
next goto the arc console and make a new boot item, set the osloader to \linload.exe and then the boot image to \avanti<br>
<br>
next set the boot options to boot fd0:xl.gz root=/dev/fd0 prompt_ramdisk=1 load_ramdisk=1<br>
<br>
3) snag the redhat xl.gz image and just copy it to a fat disk<br>
<br>
4) snag the ramdisk.img and rawrite that to a disk.<br>
<br>
5) boot the redhat, as soon as milo is done loading insert your disk with xl.gz on it....<br>
<br>
6) after xl.gz goes though it should prompt you for a root floppy, pop that sucker in and boom the menu should come up<br>
<br>
NOTICE how i said should =]<br>
<br>
<br>
P.S. Thanks to everyone who pushed me thought it =]</font><br>
</html>


