What are you comparing to?  Many JVM's have been highly optimized for 
Intel, with tight assembly code and fast JIT compilers.

I believe AXP can have outstanding java performance, but few people have 
attempted the necessary optimizations.  Sometime last year there was an 
attempt to build a JVM exclusively for Alpha from scratch 
(http://www.complang.tuwien.ac.at/java/cacao), but it seems to have stalled.
Their early results were impressive though.

The key to java performance on AXP is to somehow transform the JVM stack 
machine into a register machine.  This is best done with JIT technology.
There is an interesting JIT project for Linux/Intel called TYA.  I haven't
heard of anyone trying to port it to AXP, but it might be a good starting
point...


Jeff

