On Wednesday, July 15, 1998 5:08 AM, Hirsim{ki Mika [SMTP:mhi@alpha.cc.tut.fi] wrote:
------------- stuff deleted -------------------------------
> it started beeping. There are six beeps, a pause, six beeps,
> etc.
> 
> According to the manual it's trying to tell me that "Checksum
> error detected when image was read back from memory". The manual 
> doesn't elaborate on the subject, but I assumed that this means 
> AlphaBIOS image is somehow corrupted.
> 
------------- stuff deleted -------------------------------

Very likely a memory problem.  I just had one of these today.  We were
setting up an LX motherboard and got the 6 beeps.  Had some bad DIMM's.

If your motherboard has 4 DIMM's installed, remove the 2 closest to
the CPU and see if it will startup without the 6 beeps.  If you only
have two installed try moving them into the other DIMM sockets (not very
likely the problem but who knows).  Or try to get some known good memory to
