This is a known problem on the AlphaPC164-UX/BX, because of the funky way
that MILO is booted in pieces on that platform.

I am working on a fix along with the folks at Deskstation, who did the
original work to get LINUX running on their RPX164-2 motherboard (it's
nearly identical to the UX/BX).

For now, unfortunately, you have to live with it... :-\

