> When I thought that my new kernel was ok and I attempted a reboot,
> I obtained this:
> 
> Unable to handle kernel paging request at virtual address 0000000000210000
> reboot(724): Oops 1

I managed to solve this myself.  It was apparently a problem with
the RUFFIAN port in the 2.0.34 gatekeeper sources.
Copying from the original 2.0.30 Deskstation port, I added

#if defined(CONFIG_ALPHA_PYXIS)
        *(int *) PYXIS_RESET = 0x0000dead;
        mb();
#endif

just before the halt() statement at the end of function hard_reset_now 
in arch/alpha/kernel/process.c , and added

#define PYXIS_RESET                     (IDENT_ADDR + 0x8780000900UL)

in include/asm-alpha/pyxis.h.
Now it reboots regularly.  I do not have the faintest idea about
the meaning of what I did ;-)

furio ercolessi
