>       going to ARC first (and waiting for a keypress?), e.g. rebooting after 
>       a Power Failure?

Our machine has always BOOTed automatically following a RESET,
so for me the patch was effective in giving what you are looking for.
Yes, it goes to ARC first, but it does not wait for keypresses.
The default boot option must point to a LDMILO.EXE installed
in a bootable partition on a hard disk, example:
OsLoader = scsi(0)disk(0)rdisk(0)partition(1)\ldmilo.exe
and this in turn calls MILO with appropriate arguments, example:
OsLoadOptions = boot sda2:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/sda6 
(this is what i use, i made a second small partition for
the booting kernel just for extra safety).
The details are more or less those given in
http://www.deskstation.com/linux/boot.html

furio ercolessi
