I've been trying to ignore this thread. The customer votes with his money,
management makes decisions about the company. I had to force a manager to
fire me in support of this concept years ago.

That said, I've had trouble with Red Hat quality and support for the alpha
platform. I had installation woes with 5.1, and submitted a trouble
ticket, but I never got a decent, human response from Red Hat (I did
manage to work my way around the difficulties). I understand lack of
resources and time contraints, "been there done that", but I also know
that such occurances do not cause warm fuzzies for the customer. So QC/QA,
support need to improve (no problem, this is _always_ true, even for
insane outfits like L.L.Bean)

