a son with an axp who might start fixing some things I cann't 8-)) which
could use addressing. Like a workable graphical browser (I have failed in
my efforts so far to get one). lyx is a package I'd like to get running,
and have failed at also. Also getting wav files to play against my UDB
(sox doesn't want to convert stuff to au for me with the collection of
files I've got). 

Maybe, just possibly, if we let Red Hat alone to make their own mistakes
(which they will), we can use our energies to getting more packages into
running shape for the axp processor. It will not be smooth, just look at
the history of this list to see how many ways we can disagree, but perhaps
we can get gloriously past the critical mass to keep our platform ahead of
MS & Intel technically and commercially viable for the next 15-20 years.

