I recently moved from Redhat 5.0 on my AlphaStation 200 to DEC Unix 4.0D,
solely for the purpose of having a stable machine to run Netscape on.  However,
DU is less to my liking - RAM hog, mediocre video card support, etc.  

How stable is Netscape for OSF when running under DEC UNIX compatibility? I've
(legally) got the libs and everything (since DU4 is installed and I'm running
it right now), so I can copy the libs to a 'safe place' and then whack this
install and put 5.1 on.

(I had problems with netscape hosing my network interface randomly under
 RedHat 5.0).

If I can get DU netscape running stably under RedHat 5.1, I'll be a happy
camper (using alternate window managers like WindowMaker is a PITA under
 DU, and it sucks up ALL of my RAM with lots of various "accessory" programs;
I dont want to have to spend a week tweaking a box just to free up RAM).

Also, how's the support for the 24bit (8mb) TGA cards coming along?  I've
got a ZLXp-E2 sitting here, ready to replace this 2mb Trio64, if the 
drivers are good....

