Greetings,

	I built an RPM of net-tools-1.45 for AXP and found a few
interesting things.  First, HAVE_FW_MASQUERADE seemed to be required but
not defined anywhere, so I removed it (masquerade support is always
compiled in now).  Second, and more interesting, there were some alignment
problems with masquerade support for netstat where IP addrs were being cast
to unsigned long in a fscanf.  My glibc doesn't have support for packet
radio, so no packet radio (or ipv6 or fddi) support is built in.
Everything else should be.
