Hi Chis !

> 	IIRC, ECC has 4bits parity for every 8bits data.
> Anyone confirm or shootdown?

shootdown -h now ;-}

Parity is normally 1bit/8Bit data and dedects an odd number of
flipped bits; but can't correct them.

ECC (on alpha) works with 64-bit/Data 8-bit/"parity" (so it needs the same
number of bits like parity checking, but operates on larger junks).
ECC is able to dedect and correct a single bit error and dedects
double bit errors.

