Which version of redhat and gcc are you using?  There was a bug in
gcc where it did not handle cvttq instructions correctly, even with
-mieee enabled.  This bug was fixed in egcs.

What you should do is compile the code with -mieee, then run it
under gdb and catch the sigfpe.  Then take the faulting PC and
disassemble the dozen instructions around it and see if you can
spot a likely candidate (e.g. a floating point instruction that
does not have the "/s" flag specified).  Let us know what you find.

