It's a new file, so this indicates you may not have patched correctly.

When applying the patches, you MUST do it from inside the source tree you
are patching; for example:

	cd /usr/local/src
	tar xzf /somewhere/linux-2.0.34.tar.gz
	mv linux linux-2.0.34
	cd linux-2.0.34
	zcat /somewhere/alpha-patches-2.0.34-0.1.gz | patch -p1 -E >& ../34.log

The critical parts are the "cd linux-2.0.34" and the "patch -p1".

OTOH, you could have simply downloaded the alpha-sources-2.0.34-tar.gz, and
avoided this whole mess... ;-}

Good luck.

