Jay is correct: the XL300 uses an EV5, whereas the XL366 uses EV56.

One other important point: it is *not* possible to swap out the XL300
CPU daughtercard to upgrade to an XL366, as EV56 requires a power supply
voltage not available in the XL300 chassis.  On the other hand, there is
also an XL433, and I believe (but am not sure) that this is a possible
upgrade from XL366, if you can find the daughtercard at affordable price
of course.

