Jochen Decker wrote:

>  Has somebody tried to install a miro pctv card under
> linux/alpha???I've installed the driver, but xawtv hangs after
> starting. I've commented in main.c line 1525: /*
> XF86VidModeGetAllModeLines(dpy,XDefaultScreen(dpy),
>            &vm_count,&vm_modelines);*/Now xawtv doesn't hangs, but it
> shows only a black windows ...Could somebody help me? Bye Jochen

 Hi Jochen,

the problem is that the driver does not find out the address of the
video ram correctly.
Take a look at /proc/pci for the address (it's the entry for the video
card with the buffered
access). In my case this was 0x900000 for 2.0.3x kernels and 0x980000
for
2.1.x kernels.
Pass the first to ciphers of the address to the bttv module when
loading, e.g

insmod bttv vidmem=0x90

I had another problem with the tuner module which did not recognise my
tuner chip. You can specify this as well

insmod tuner type=5     # look at the sources for the numbers

Hope this helps!
Chris

