Hi Wes, Brian !

> Brian Wood wrote:
> > 
> > I want to add a second SCSI adapter to my SX164 machine. I know in the
> > Intel world I need to use Lilo to pass the parameters at boot.
> > 
> > Would I do the same thing using MILO? Or is there another method to
> > accomplish this?
> > 
> 
> I use two Symbios 810's and didn't add any special
> parms at boot...

This is correct for PCI cards, because dedection is very easy.
For ISA cards, there may be a need for adding this.
Anyway, if you need options, do it the Intel way.

If you have two NCR controller in the machine and the scanning order
is wrong, you can solve this in two ways:

1) Exchange the cards, because ordering is SLOT-number based.
2) add ncr53c8xx=revprob:y to the MILO commandline

If you use an NCR for internal devices and the second one for
external devices (and you plug'n play a lot) the first 
solution is better, because loading MILO itself may be
a problem, when you have a external disk...

