the machine
almost immediatly. The rest (floppy, SHM, sound) was working fine. Video
for Linux
was ok.

RedHat 2.0.34: aic7xxx liked my disk, RAID-0 worked, but the floppy
didn't work anymore for unknown reasons. Sound didn't work either
(DMA/IRQ timeout),
and SHM was broken as well (the MIT SHM of X didn't work anymore). Video
for Linux
was ok.

Jay's 2.0.34-1: aic7xxx failed after probing my CDROM after startup. For
this reason I cannot
tell about the other things that did not work anymore in RedHat 2.0.34.

Pristine 2.1.107: aic7xxx liked my disk, RAID-0 worked, sound and SHM
worked
also, but floppy was broken again. Video for Linux was ok.

2.1.109 with d-axp-109 patches: aic7xxx and RAID-0 were ok, sound did
not work
(DMA/IRQ timeout), floppy broken as well. SHM was ok. Video for Linux
did not
work anymore.

I haven't looked at 2.0.35 yet (but I expect the floppy to not work).

My sytem is a SX164 with 64MB RAM, Adaptec 2940UW SCSI card, two IBM
DCAS
(2GB, ultra, not wide), Matrox Mystique-220, Soundblaster SB16 PnP,
Hauppauge PCI
TV card, Planet PCI NE2000 card, MILO-2.0.30 from gatekeeper.dec.com.

I understand that I cannot expect a fully working system for 2.1.x
kernels, but I thought
for the "stable" 2.0.x kernel quite everything should work fine.

Any hints, or somebody with similar problems?

Thanks you,

Chris

