Content-Type: text/plain; charset=us-ascii
X-Mailer: Mutt 0.91.1

Has anybody else noticed that the netcfg option on the ppp connection that
says "Escape control character" does the exact opposite of what it's supposed
to do?  If you check off that box, it sets 
ESCAPECHARS=yes
in /etc/sysconfig/network-scripts/ifcfg-ppp0.  And in
/etc/sysconfig/network-scripts/ifup-ppp, it uses that value to add the option
if [ "${ESCAPECHARS}" = yes ] ; then
  opts="$opts asyncmap 00000000"
fi
The only problem with that is that setting asyncmap to 000000 tells it NOT TO
ESCAPE ANY CHARACTERS!!!  Leaving the option off entirely tells it to escape
the regular control characters.

