On Wed, 22 Jul 1998, Dumb Kid wrote:

> Anyone tried iBCS emulation on Linux/Alpha?? There is
> a rpm for i386 Redhat5.x, but I don't see one for Alpha.

iBCS doesn't work on any platform other than Intel.  That is because it
stands for Intel Binary Compatibility Specification. :)  However, you can
run Digital Unix binaries and Intel Linux binaries (through CPU emulation)
on Linux/Alpha.  But I wouldn't expect to get for example, SCO binaries to
run through iBCS emulation through x86 emulation.  iBCS is a kernel module
and I doubt that the Alpha kernel would work with it.  (the Alpha kernels
have enough trouble even running software on the aptly named Alpha
platform :) ).


