> If iBCS emulation is not an option, how does one execute
> an SCO binary in Linux/Alpha??

As of the moment, you can't.

Compiling the ibcs code won't do you very much good; since Alpha
is a different CPU architecture than Intel, you can't execute 
SCO binaries directly on an Alpha system.  You need something like
em86 to make it all work.

I've been meaning to add ibcs emulation support to em86 and
improve the packaging thereof, but round tuits are hard to come
by...  I have some major items to clear off my plate this summer,
but I hope that by fall I'll be able to get back to some hacking
on em86 for just this purpose.

