On Thu, 23 Jul 1998, Jim Paradis wrote:

> Here's what needs to be done.  I don't know if I'll have the time to
> do it soon, but if anyone else wants to give it a shot, be my guest.
> 
> First, pull all the required shared libraries over into /usr/x86/lib
> on your alpha system.
> 
> Second, you need to crock up a version of ld-linux.so.2 which uses
> /usr/x86 as its default library path.  This *should* be a simple
> source code change and rebuild.
> 
> Finally, run ldconfig86 on the alpha system.


