> I presume this is a problem with IRQ, but have not been able to fix
> it, even if I compile a minimal kernel (without even network drivers).
> Does anyone have experience of this/know how to fix it? It's so
> annoying, because I know it wants to work!

I have a 100% fix for you: Just uncomment (/* SMP = 1 */) in the
Makefile and you'll be saved !!!!
The message can only appear if compiled with SMP enabled; this 
is a questionable idea on LX. (ok, I looked into 2.1.110, so I
don't know if it's also true for 2.1.103).
Compiling __SMP__ on 2.1.xx is _not_ a good idea at moment, 
because the SMP stuff is not adapted for 2.1.xxx.

BTW: please don't use 2.1.103 anymore.
Use 2.1.110+rth patch posted two days ago.
Report any problems here to the list; I've reported already one 
for LX (console-switching out of X11 crashes here).

!!!! Please !!!!
It's very important to test 2.1.xxx kernels on all platforms
(Tsunami too ;-}). 
The current "stable" development release is 2.1.110 + rth patch.

thank you, 
