>>> Jordan said:
> 
> I am using SRM, and if I can install a boot block then it would solve all of
> my problems. On x86 lilo install it's self into the mbr or the superblock,
> what program do I use to do this on RH5.0 (Alpha) ???

Refer to the Alpha FAQ pages on SRM booting at:

	www.azstarnet.com/~axplinux/srm.html

Basically, you reseve 1024 sectors in front of the first partition, and then
run "swriteboot" to write the boot strap program, aboot, into that area.

> One other thing. When I do a "show device" at the SRM console I get a line
> like this:
> 
> dka0.0.0.6.0		DKA0		RZ26F	1Q04
> 
> Could you shed a little light one the meaning of the of the numbering system
> of the numbers which follow dka in the first element of the table ???

Sorry, I didn't understand them when I worked in the DU group and booted
from SRM all the time... ;-}

--Jay++

