>>> Derrick J Brashear said:
> 
> The state of MILO as I know it:
> Most available MILOs for the avanti: when run, you get a green screen
>   where you can see nothing

This is only true on AVANTIs equipped with the 24-plane TGA (ZLXp-E2).

> milo-avanti-980606: cursor is correct, but when attempting to boot a
>   kernel we get ...Fatal error: not enough memory on at least two machines
>   we tried

Uh, how much memory do you have in those systems? It may not work in 16Mb...

The cursor problems stem, I believe, from differences in the setup of the TGA
by ARC and by SRM; I'd be real interested to know just what it is that is
different, so if anyone would like to play detective... ;-}

> The milo available from the debian-alpha milo developer whose name escapes
>   me: readable screen, cursor has same (8 chars wide) problem, when scroll
>   becomes necessary things get goofy.

I'm working with Nikita Schmidt to resolve these issues, and integrate his
enhancements into my MILO sources.

> a) maybe the patches which make the cursor work correctly in
> milo-avanti-980606 could be made available? I'd ask the person who did
> them, but I can't find any announcement of where this milo came from, only
> after-the-fact statements.

See the end for the set of patches I used for tga.c; basically, the kernel
sources worked pretty well, so I simply back-ported them into the MILO
sources.

> I've heard reports from others that milo-avanti-980606 worked for them.
> I'm curious what's different about our hardware, but since I have
> something that almost works, I haven't pursued it.

I'm curious too; how about posting a /proc/cpuinfo and /proc/pci from it?

--Jay++

