On Fri, 24 Jul 1998 Maciej W. Rozycki wrote:
>On Fri, 24 Jul 1998, Eric Hilton Jones wrote:
>
>>   I was curious, in the past I have just created a directory for new
>> versions of egcs to run from to keep the gcc installed with redhat and=
 the
>> new versions seperate. Has anyone had any problems upgrading the egcs
>> compiler that comes with 5.1 to a newer version?
>
> You may always install several versions of gcc in it's usual place
>('/usr/lib/gcc-lib') and select any of them using gcc's '-V' option.  No=
te
>that gcc ('/usr/bin/gcc') is only a driver; it's version doesn't matter.=
=20

Yeah, but you have to be carefu about the libs that come with the compile=
rs.
gcc-2.8.1 and egcs are using the same sonames for their libraries, which =
are
different ! So you should not install gcc-2.8 and egcs into one directory=
 !

